{"timestamp": 1779385600.165472, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 10, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "weapons", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779385600.166281, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 10, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779385605.991931, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Alice's body in weapons. I just arrived there from cafeteria when I saw her dead next to me.\n\nMy route was: cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons. While I was in medbay (ticks 3-5), Frank was there with me \u2014 he came in from storage. So Frank has at least a partial alibi from me for those ticks.\n\nI didn't see anyone else on my path. Whoever was in weapons before me, or came from the cafeteria/security side, is suspicious. I'd like to hear from Charlie, Diana, and Eve about where they were \u2014 especially anyone who can account for being near weapons."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385613.71472, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was medbay \u2192 storage \u2192 lower engine. I was in medbay early, then headed to storage around tick 4 where I saw Diana \u2014 she came in from lower engine. I stayed with Diana in storage through ticks 4-6, then moved to lower engine to do my task there.\n\nSo Diana has an alibi from me for ticks 4-6 in storage, and she came from lower engine \u2014 nowhere near weapons. I never went anywhere near weapons or cafeteria, so I couldn't have killed Alice.\n\nThat means we should focus on Eve, since neither Bob nor I saw her. Frank was with Bob in medbay, Diana was with me in storage. Eve is the only one unaccounted for. I'd like to hear her route."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385635.4209569, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I started upper engine, went up to oxygen, then through cafeteria toward the right side. I did pass through weapons briefly and Alice was alive there when I saw her \u2014 I didn\u2019t see anyone else with her. After that I went down to security to do/check cams, and that\u2019s where I was when the report happened.\n\nSo yeah, I was near weapons, but Alice was alive when I left. Charlie jumping straight to \u201cit must be Eve\u201d feels a little too neat when he\u2019s basing it only on who he personally saw. I\u2019d like to hear Diana and Frank\u2019s exact timings too, because someone could\u2019ve come from cafeteria or security after I left."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385642.032151, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Confirming Charlie's story: I started in lower engine, moved to storage where I met Charlie at tick 4. We were together in storage through ticks 4-5, and at tick 6 I saw him leave toward lower engine. After that I headed up to medbay.\n\nSo Charlie and I alibi each other for that window, and neither of us was anywhere near weapons.\n\nThat leaves Eve as the most suspicious \u2014 she openly admits she was in weapons with Alice, and no one can verify what happened after. Her deflection onto Charlie is weak; Charlie's reasoning isn't \"too neat,\" it's just process of elimination, and it lines up with what I saw.\n\nFrank, I'd like to hear your route to close the loop, but right now I'm leaning Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385649.091361, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route was storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical. I can confirm Bob's story \u2014 I was in medbay with him at ticks 3 and 4, and at tick 5 I saw him leave toward electrical. That matches his stated route exactly (cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons), so Bob's clear in my book.\n\nThat also means I'm cleared by Bob for the medbay window, and I went to electrical after \u2014 nowhere near weapons.\n\nSo we have: Bob and I alibi each other, Charlie and Diana alibi each other. Eve is the only one without a witness, and by her own admission she was in weapons with Alice right before the body was found. Her attempt to cast doubt on Charlie's reasoning doesn't change the fact that she places herself at the crime scene.\n\nI'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385655.3920472, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Thanks everyone for laying out routes. To recap mine clearly: cafeteria \u2192 medbay (ticks 3-5, with Frank) \u2192 electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons, where I found Alice dead the moment I walked in.\n\nFrank confirms my medbay window, Charlie and Diana alibi each other in storage/lower engine, and Frank went to electrical \u2014 none of them were near weapons in the kill window.\n\nEve, by her own admission, was in weapons with Alice and says Alice was alive when she left. The problem is there's no one to corroborate that, and she's the only person whose path puts her at the crime scene. Her pivot to questioning Charlie's reasoning doesn't give her an alibi \u2014 it just deflects.\n\nI'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385659.490178, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Eve placed herself in weapons with Alice and has no one to back up her claim that Alice was alive when she left. Everyone else has a mutual alibi \u2014 Bob/Frank in medbay, me/Diana in storage. Eve's deflection onto me doesn't change the fact that she's the only one at the crime scene in the kill window. I'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385685.6697202, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019m telling you all, the \u201ceveryone has an alibi\u201d thing is being overstated. Those alibis are for early ticks \u2014 Bob/Frank in medbay around 3-5, Charlie/Diana in storage around 4-6. I saw Alice alive in weapons at tick 7, so the kill had to happen after that.\n\nI left weapons and went straight down to security. Bob says he went electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons and found the body. That route puts him entering weapons after my sighting, with no one actually watching him at the moment he \u201cfound\u201d it. Reporter doesn\u2019t automatically mean clear \u2014 self-reports happen.\n\nIf I killed Alice, why would I openly admit I was in weapons and say she was alive? I\u2019m giving the timing that narrows the window. The person whose own route ends at the body after Alice was alive is Bob. Please don\u2019t just tunnel me because I\u2019m the only one being honest about seeing Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385693.270304, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Eve, your counter-argument has a problem: Bob was with Frank in medbay through tick 5, then went electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons. Frank independently confirmed Bob's medbay window, so Bob's route is corroborated up to tick 5. The remaining travel time to weapons fits the kill window you're describing \u2014 but so does yours, and you're the one who placed yourself in weapons with Alice.\n\nThe key difference: Bob has Frank vouching for the first half of his route. You have nobody vouching for any part of yours. \"Why would I admit I was there\" isn't an alibi \u2014 sometimes admitting the unavoidable is the only play when you think someone might have seen you.\n\nI'm sticking with Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385700.982236, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I've already laid out my route and analysis \u2014 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical, with Bob confirmed alongside me in medbay ticks 3-4 and leaving toward electrical at tick 5.\n\nEve, your pivot to Bob doesn't hold up. Bob's first half is corroborated by me, and his stated route (electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons) is a clean continuation. You, on the other hand, have zero corroboration for any part of your route, and you place yourself at the crime scene right before the kill. \"I admitted it so I must be innocent\" is not an alibi \u2014 it's spin.\n\nBob/Frank alibi each other, Charlie/Diana alibi each other. You're the odd one out, and you're at the scene. I'm voting Eve."}}
